menu "Bind Bandit (ESP32 Classic-BT Host)"

config JOYCON_HOST_NAME_SUBSTR
    string "Target device name substring"
    default "Joy-Con"
    help
        Substring match against discovered device names.
        For Binbok / third-party controllers you may need to change this
        (e.g. "Binbok", "Pro Controller", etc.).

config JOYCON_HOST_DISCOVERY_SECONDS
    int "Inquiry scan duration (seconds)"
    range 1 60
    default 10
    help
        How long each Bluetooth inquiry scan should run.

config JOYCON_HOST_LOG_REPORTS
    bool "Log HID input reports (on change)"
    default y
    help
        When enabled, logs input report bytes when they change.
        This is the evidence-first workflow for implementing a correct mapper.

config JOYCON_HOST_UART_DEBUG_REPORTS
    bool "Forward raw HID reports over UART (debug frames)"
    default n
    help
        When enabled, raw HID reports are also forwarded over the existing UART
        framing (length > 1). The ESP32-S3 receiver ignores these frames.
        Use this only for offline capture with a USB-UART dongle.

config JOYCON_HOST_UART_DEBUG_MAX_BYTES
    int "Max HID report bytes to forward"
    range 8 200
    default 48
    depends on JOYCON_HOST_UART_DEBUG_REPORTS
    help
        HID reports can be long; forward only the first N bytes.

config JOYCON_HOST_TRY_NINTENDO_0X30
    bool "Try parse Nintendo-style 0x30 reports (candidate, optional)"
    default n
    help
        When enabled, the mapper will attempt to parse reports that match a common
        Nintendo-style signature (report_id=0x30). This is useful as a hint when
        you are capturing evidence and want higher-level fields (buttons/sticks)
        printed for validation.

        It stays conservative:
        - It only activates when the signature matches.
        - It does not guess other layouts.

config JOYCON_HOST_NINTENDO_0X30_EMIT_KEYS
    bool "Emit key events from parsed 0x30 reports (advanced)"
    default n
    depends on JOYCON_HOST_TRY_NINTENDO_0X30
    help
        When enabled, the mapper will emit KEY_ID_* events from parsed stick data.
        Keep this OFF until you've verified that the parsed fields match your
        actual controller by comparing with raw report bytes.

config JOYCON_HOST_AUTO_RECONNECT
    bool "Auto-reconnect on BT disconnect"
    default y
    help
        When enabled, the ESP32 will automatically attempt to re-connect to the
        last known controller BDA after a disconnect. Uses exponential backoff
        (2s, 4s, 8s) for up to 3 retries before falling back to discovery.

config JOYCON_HOST_AUTO_RECONNECT_MAX_RETRIES
    int "Max auto-reconnect retries"
    range 1 10
    default 3
    depends on JOYCON_HOST_AUTO_RECONNECT
    help
        Number of reconnect attempts before giving up and restarting discovery.

endmenu
